# The Dockerfile copies exactly what it builds — CMakeLists.txt, src, go.mod, go.sum, cmd,
# internal — so everything else is context the daemon transfers and never reads.
#
# `build/` and `ui/node_modules/` are the two that matter: together they are an order of magnitude
# larger than the source, and `build/` also carries a host-toolchain CMake cache that would be
# actively wrong inside the image if anything ever copied it.
.git
.cache
build
ui
docs
legacy
testing
scripts
deployment
*.md
*.db
compile_commands.json
Dockerfile*
Makefile
LICENSE
